id: E429
error_signature: test failure: backtrace test functions optimized away despite __attribute__((noclone))
match_keywords: noclone,sibling-calls,omit-frame-pointer,backtrace,test,tail-call-optimization
category: compiler-optimization,testing
severity: medium
root_cause: Clang on OHOS aarch64 ignores GCC-specific __attribute__((noclone)), causing test functions (e.g., callback_one, callback_two in libbacktrace test suite) to be optimized via tail call elimination or frame pointer omission. This breaks backtrace stack frame tests that expect distinct function entries.
rec_approach: Add -fno-optimize-sibling-calls and -fno-omit-frame-pointer to CFLAGS for test compilation targets only (not the library itself). In Makefile-based builds, use TEST_CFLAGS or target-specific CFLAGS; in CMake, set COMPILE_FLAGS on test targets.
solution_cmds: |
  # Makefile approach (libbacktrace)
  export TEST_CFLAGS="-fno-optimize-sibling-calls -fno-omit-frame-pointer"
  # Apply to test objects only, e.g.:
  # btest_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) $(TEST_CFLAGS)
  # stest_CFLAGS = $(AM_CFLAGS) $(TEST_CFLAGS)
verification: Run `make check` and verify tests like backtrace_simple_test, backtrace_full_test pass with correct stack frame counts (e.g., 33/33 for libbacktrace). Check test logs for "backtrace" lines showing expected function names.
fallback: If flags insufficient, consider using volatile variables or inline assembly barriers in test code to prevent optimization, though this modifies upstream sources.
doc_refs: E077,E129
applies_to: libbacktrace,any-backtrace-testing-library
last_updated: 2026-09-02
